# Incident bundles are written by the Local Agent every time a task ends
# abnormally, so on any machine that runs the product this directory fills with
# one file per failure — 13 of them accumulated in a single session of restarting
# the agent. They also carry the user's task text verbatim, which is not something
# to commit by accident.
#
# The eight bundles that ARE tracked were curated evidence attached to a change
# (see the commits that added them). Keeping that convention means adding a new
# one deliberately: `git add -f artifacts/incidents/<id>.bundle.json`.
# Already-tracked files are unaffected by this rule.
/artifacts/incidents/*.bundle.json

# Scratch space for live verification runs: copies of real agent databases,
# build artifacts and probe programs written while checking a behaviour against a
# running system. Nothing here is a deliverable, and a copied agent.db is over a
# hundred megabytes of somebody's task history.
/artifacts/scratch/
/artifacts/robocasa*/
!/artifacts/robocasa-harness/
/artifacts/robocasa-harness/*
!/artifacts/robocasa-harness/round3/
!/artifacts/robocasa-harness/round3/**
!/artifacts/robocasa-harness/round4/
!/artifacts/robocasa-harness/round4/**
/artifacts/sim-stack/
# Recorded by scripts/start-all.sh so `down` stops exactly what `up` started.
/artifacts/start-all/
# Guided calibration sessions: per-unit measurements made on a specific robot.
/artifacts/calibration/
# Built maps: surveys of a specific building, often large binaries.
/artifacts/maps/
# Redundant scans moved aside rather than deleted, so nothing referenced is lost.
/artifacts/maps-archive/
# Frozen sensor logs: hundreds of megabytes of raw frames from one building, which a
# fresh recording regenerates. The format is code (robot/gateway/.../sensor_log.py) and
# the recorder is a script, so what is deliberately not kept here is the data itself.
/artifacts/replay/
# The survey benchmark's rasterised ground truth for the same reason.
/artifacts/benchmark/
/artifacts/gazebo-house/
/artifacts/sim-assets/
/artifacts/training/
# Browser-regression output from scripts/check-console-ui.cjs and
# scripts/check-scene-views.cjs (regenerate locally; see docs/frontend/console-v1.md).
/artifacts/ui-v1/
/artifacts/task3-console-live.jpg
